  "worked_solution": "Both the numerator and denominator approach $\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$ However, since ${e}^{x/4}\u226b\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(x+1)$ for large values of $x,$ the numerator is growing much faster than the denominator. Consequently, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{e}^{x/4}}{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(x+1)}=\\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{{e}^{x/4}}{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(x+1)}-2)=\\infty .\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
